%S A399516 1,2,4,7,10,14,19,25,32,39,47,56,66,77,88,100,113,127,142,158,175,192,
%T A399516 210,229,249,270,292,315,338,362,387,413,440,468,497,527,558,589,621,
%U A399516 654,688,723,759,796,834,873,912,952,993,1035,1078,1122,1167,1213,1260,1308,1357
%N A399516 Indices of jumps in A399515, where first differences A399515(n+1) - A399515(n) are > 1.
%C A399516 Sequence A399515 lists numbers a for which there are smaller integers b > c = sqrt(a + d) > d = sqrt(b + c) > 0. The sequence has increasingly long runs of consecutive integers which are interrupted by increasingly large jumps, whose indices are listed here.
%C A399516 The jumps occur in A399515 around squares > 4^2 = 16, i.e., A399515(a(n)) < (n+3)^2 < A399515(a(n)+1). The gaps g(n) = A399515(a(n)+1) - A399515(a(n)) form the sequence 8, 10, 11, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 20, 21, ... of all integers >= 8 except for the integers 9, 13, 19, ... = A080827(4..) = A099392(5..).
%F A399516 a(n) <= A196126(n) with equality up to a(n = 14) = 77, and strict inequality for n >= 15.
%F A399516 a(n) <= A281706(n-4)-1 with equality up to a(n = 13) = 66, and strict inequality for n >= 14.
%o A399516 (PARI) A399516(first=99)=my(d=99,a=0,n=-1);vector(first,i, until(1+d<d=a, until(is_A399515(a++),); n++);n)
%Y A399516 Cf. A399515.
%K A399516 nonn
%O A399516 1,2
